<title>SINGAPORE: First Engineering half year net slips.</title>
<headline>First Engineering half year net slips.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  0.85     vs     1.14</p>
<p>    Group share ($)		   1.20     vs     1.60</p>
<p>    Turnover			   40.15     vs    20.09</p>
<p>    Other income			0.78     vs     0.10</p>
<p>    Interest expense		  0.58     vs     0.38</p>
<p>    Depreciation, amortisation    1.53     vs     1.37</p>
<p>    Associates			 (0.05)    vs    (0.08)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    1.09     vs     1.41</p>
<p>    Tax				   0.08     vs     0.19</p>
<p>    Minorities			 (0.11)    vs     nil</p>
<p>Note - First Engineering Ltd said profits were eroded by reduced margins from assembly activity, difficult market conditions, intense competition and a price cut in a major project. It said group performance would continue to be affected by high overhead costs, the slowdown in the electronics industry and increased competition.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
